# Cloudflare Pages caching — guarantee visitors never get a stale page.
#
# Every file is revalidated on each visit: the browser sends a conditional
# request and gets a cheap "304 Not Modified" when nothing changed, or the new
# file immediately after a deploy. Next.js build assets are content-hashed, so
# their revalidations are trivial 304s and correctness is guaranteed.
#
# (We intentionally use a single rule. Cloudflare Pages APPENDS the headers of
# every matching rule, so a catch-all plus a more specific "/_next/static/*"
# rule produces one conflicting Cache-Control — avoided by keeping just this.)
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
